rem Squarefree Binomial Coefficients
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=203
rem Sum the distinct squarefree numbers
rem in the first Rows rows of Pascal's
rem triangle

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Rows integer = 51

rem K is clipped to the row, which only
rem repeats values of that row. A
rem coefficient has only prime factors
rem below Rows, so it is squarefree when
rem no prime square divides it.
N = 0 till Rows array
Row = N reshape Rows 1
Grid' = Row (N Row min) binomial
Vals = Grid reshape (Rows * Rows) unique
Sq = (primes till Rows array) ** 2
Col' = Vals reshape (Vals len) 1
Div' = Col mod Sq equal 0
Free' = not (Div any axis 1)
Kept' = Vals filter Free
Answer = Kept sum
Answer print
